Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(schema): one value in brackets is his note; a default
 never replaces it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red at 917c70e:
  a-bracket-is-his-answers "a single value in brackets is a note, not a
  list of options":
    field('جدول المنتجات فيه اسم الصنف والسعر والحالة (متوفر)', 'الحالة').options
    Received: ["قيد الانتظار", "قيد الإصلاح", "تم الإصلاح"]

Culprit (bisected): 75e32c75. It made every state-named label a select
with a default lifecycle (TYPE_MARKS status mark + default options in
fieldsFromLabels) so "repair status" gets a real filter contract
(directory-request-contract). The bracket reader already refused to turn
ONE bracketed value into options, but the default then filled the column
anyway - with three repair-shop states that cannot even hold «متوفر», the
one answer he wrote. A default fills a silence; here he spoke.
Decision: R. The bracket reader records the labels he followed with a
single value (`noted`), and fieldsFromLabels skips the state mark for
those labels only, so the column stays his free text (as it read before
the defaults existed). The state mark is named (NAMES_A_STATE) so the skip
is explicit. 75e32c75's own contract is kept: a state he leaves open still
gets its default lifecycle, and two or more bracketed values are still his
options. Added both halves to the suite: the noted column still exists and
is text; and NEGATIVE - a bare «الحالة» is still a select with >= 2 options.

Mutation evidence (mutate.py, sha256 identical after each):
  M6 skip removed (default overrides his note):
    ✕ a single value in brackets is a note, not a list of options
      Received: ["قيد الانتظار", "قيد الإصلاح", "تم الإصلاح"]
    ✕ …and the note keeps the column, as his free text
      Expected: "text"  Received: "select"
  M7 skip widened to every state column:
    ✕ NEGATIVE — a state he left open still gets its default lifecycle
      Expected: "select"  Received: "text"
    ✕ directory-request-contract: turns the named status into a real
      filter contract  Expected: "flag1"  Received: "text3"

